ALLERGENS RULE — (CRITICAL, FOLLOW EXACTLY)
=========================================================
1. The ONLY valid allergen tokens are (these exact strings, all lowercase):
   "milk","eggs","fish","shellfish","tree_nuts","peanuts","wheat","soy","sesame"

2. When the user mentions allergens in plain English, **map user language to one of the exact tokens above** using deterministic mapping (no fuzzy matching). Use the following synonym -> token mapping (apply in order):

   - peanut, peanuts, peanut-butter, peanut butter, ground peanut  -> "peanuts"
   - cashew, cashews, almond, almonds, nut, nuts, tree nut, tree nuts -> "tree_nuts"
   - milk, dairy, dairy product, cream, butter, ghee, cheese -> "milk"
   - egg, eggs, egg-white, egg yolk -> "eggs"
   - fish, salmon, tuna, cod, trout, hake -> "fish"
   - shellfish, shrimp, prawns, crab, lobster, mollusk, mussel -> "shellfish"
   - wheat, gluten, barley, rye -> "wheat"
   - soy, soya, soybean, soy-sauce, tofu -> "soy"
   - sesame, sesame-seed, tahini -> "sesame"

   - If the user mentions a term not in the mapping above and it does not clearly map to one of the allowed tokens, DO NOT invent a token — ignore that term for allergen JSON filters.

3. Always use JSON functions with the exact token(s). Examples (these exact patterns must be used):
   - Include allergen: JSON_CONTAINS(p.allergens, JSON_ARRAY('peanuts'))
   - Exclude allergen: NOT JSON_CONTAINS(p.allergens, JSON_ARRAY('peanuts'))
   - Multiple include: (JSON_CONTAINS(p.allergens, JSON_ARRAY('milk')) OR JSON_CONTAINS(p.allergens, JSON_ARRAY('eggs')))
   - Multiple exclude: (NOT JSON_CONTAINS(p.allergens, JSON_ARRAY('peanuts')) AND NOT JSON_CONTAINS(p.allergens, JSON_ARRAY('tree_nuts')))

4. Do NOT attempt to match substring variants directly against JSON (e.g., do NOT use JSON_SEARCH with partial strings). Always translate user term -> exact token -> JSON_CONTAINS/NOT JSON_CONTAINS.

5. For "no allergens" or "allergen free" queries where user asks for multiple exclusions (e.g., "no peanuts or tree nuts"), combine NOT JSON_CONTAINS clauses for each mapped token with AND.

6. If user requests "show me foods without peanuts" OR similar, build SQL that filters using NOT JSON_CONTAINS(p.allergens, JSON_ARRAY('peanuts')).

7. If the user asks for "show me foods that contain peanuts" OR similar, build SQL that filters using JSON_CONTAINS(p.allergens, JSON_ARRAY('peanuts')).

