QUERY INTERPRETATION RULES (SUMMARY)
=========================================================

# 1. PRICE
“under $12”, “below 10 dollars”, “cheap”, “foods under 30” → fi.price <= X
If “cheap” without number → assume X = 20.

# 2. CALORIES / NUTRITION
“under 300 calories” → p.calories_kcal <= 300
"above 25g protein" → p.protein_g > 25
“high protein” → p.protein_g >= 20
“low carb” → p.carbs_g <= 20

# 3. DIET TYPES
vegan → p.is_vegan = TRUE
gluten free → p.is_gluten_free = TRUE
keto → p.carbs_g <= 25

# 4. SPICE
mild → p.spice_level = 'mild' OR p.spice_score <= 1
medium → p.spice_level = 'medium'
spicy → p.spice_score >= 3
very spicy → p.spice_score >= 4 OR p.spice_level = 'very_spicy'

# 5. CUISINE / TAGS
“Italian dishes” → r.cuisine LIKE '%italian%' OR JSON_CONTAINS(p.tags, JSON_ARRAY('italian'))

# 6. CATEGORY
“breakfast foods” → p.category_code = 'breakfast'

# 7. INGREDIENT PRESENCE / ABSENCE
“with mushrooms” → JOIN ffi / ingredients and filter LOWER(i.name) = 'mushroom'
“without onions/garlic” → use NOT EXISTS subquery checking LOWER(i.name) IN ('onion','garlic')

# 8. TEXT SEARCH
Match across fi.display_name, fi.canonical_name, fi.short_description, fi.long_description using LIKE '%term%'

# 9. ORDER / LIMIT
Only include ORDER BY / LIMIT if user explicitly asks for sorting or top N.

